# Dump files — never commit these; they contain process memory (secrets/PII).
*.dmp
*.dump

# Analysis outputs — generated at build time, case-specific. Root-anchored
# (leading /) so these patterns do NOT also swallow the byte-exact parity
# corpus (parity/fixtures/*/analysis.txt, status.json, …).
/analysis.txt
/analysis.md
/provenance.txt
/status.json

# Baked file server binary — fetched at build time from GitHub releases.
# These files were previously committed but are no longer tracked.
fileserver/

# Parity harness build output — parity/run-parity.sh publishes the .NET
# report tools here for the differential gate. Never committed; rebuilt on
# demand. (parity/run-parity.sh and parity/fixtures/ ARE tracked — they are
# the gate + its corpus.)
parity/_bin/

# Symbol cache and user PDBs — case-specific, potentially large/sensitive.
# The symbols/ directory itself IS tracked (via symbols/.keep);
# only its contents are excluded.
symbols/*
!symbols/.keep

# .NET build artifacts — when a host accidentally runs `dotnet build`/`publish`
# from within a project directory, MSBuild populates bin/ and obj/ alongside
# the .csproj. The dotnet-autopsy report tools are always built INSIDE
# throwaway SDK containers (parity/_bin or the per-image Docker layer), so
# bin/ and obj/ should never be committed. Phase E's trace/TraceTriage/ is
# the first project tree under this repo; this rule covers any future ones.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# chainguard/base.dockerfile is GENERATED by chainguard/generate.sh from
# common/base.dockerfile, but is INTENTIONALLY COMMITTED — not gitignored
# — so a fresh clone can run `./chainguard/build.sh` immediately without
# first having to run the generator. Same reasoning as the parity
# goldens being tracked: the artifact is the contract a reviewer can
# inspect on a PR, and CI doesn't have to regenerate to build.
#
# Maintenance: when common/base.dockerfile changes, run
# `./chainguard/generate.sh -y --force` and commit the regenerated
# chainguard/base.dockerfile alongside the upstream change.
#
# (Not gitignored — listed here as a documentation anchor only.)
